--- one anomaly observed in the preflight log, assessed, NOT fixed here -------
scripts/restore-test-from-baseline.sh: line 765: toast: command not found

  WHAT IT IS: `scripts/restore-test-from-baseline.sh:821` carries an UNESCAPED backtick pair
  inside the `<<TXN_CLOSURE` heredoc, whose delimiter is unquoted. Bash therefore ran
  `toast table pg_toast.pg_toast_16428` as a command and substituted its (empty) output.
  IMPACT, MEASURED not assumed: the backticks sit inside a single-line `--` SQL comment
  (the sibling occurrences at :799/:801/:847/:849 ARE escaped as `\``), so the generated
  transaction stays valid SQL and merely loses that comment's quoted text. The preflight ran
  to a byte-for-byte-equal post-census with it present.
  WHY IT IS NOT FIXED IN THIS PLAN: the fix is a source edit to a script that
  `workflow_dispatch` only runs FROM MAIN, so shipping it would require another founder merge
  between the preflight and the restore — spending the one-way door's timing on a lost code
  comment. Booked in this phase's deferred-items.md instead.

